    <string name="pet_upload_invalid">This image could not be read. Use a PNG grid with equal-size frames that split evenly across and down.</string>
    <string name="pet_upload_failed">Upload did not finish. Try again.</string>
    <string name="pet_upload_missing">That image cannot be opened. It may have been deleted, or it only exists in the cloud. Pick another, or download it to the phone first.</string>
    <string name="guide_pet_detail">Meet the pet, get a spritesheet, and put it on your phone</string>
    <string name="pet_guide_what_title">What is the pet</string>
    <string name="pet_guide_what_body">The look comes from one PNG grid: each column cell is an animation frame and each row is an action. The count need not be 8 - 4, 5, 6, 7 or 8 frames across are all detected. Row order follows the ChatGPT desktop pet contract: 1 idle, 2 running right, 3 running left, 4 waving, 5 failed, 6 waiting for you, 7 working, 8 finished, then two rows of look directions. A missing row is fine - the pet falls back to idle. A transparent background looks cleanest.</string>
    <string name="pet_guide_get_title">Where to get one</string>
    <string name="pet_guide_get_body">ChatGPT desktop pets, Shimeji pixel packs, or your own drawing. Any sheet with equal-size frames that split evenly works.</string>
    <string name="pet_guide_upload_title">How to upload</string>
    <string name="pet_guide_upload_body">Move the PNG to your phone, open Settings → Pet, and tap Upload image to pick it. The file is stored on-device, and the previous image is removed when you swap it.</string>
    <string name="pet_guide_tap_title">Tapping the pet</string>
    <string name="pet_guide_tap_body">A quick double tap opens the Xiaoman app; a single tap does nothing. Drag to move the pet anywhere on screen.</string>
